title: Chat request with an Xberg tool call
---
sequenceDiagram
  %% Source for 24-xberg-tool-call-flow.html. Edit this file, then run ./scripts/render-diagrams.py.
  %% Directives: docs in diagrams/README.md (Updating diagrams).
  %% @subtitle With server_url litellm_proxy and require_approval never, LiteLLM runs the model's Xberg extract call, screens the result, and asks the model again in the same request
  %% @type cloud: TR
  %% @type security: PR EG
  %% @type external: OAI WEB
  %% @type database: OBS
  actor C as Client / agent
  participant TR as Traefik<br/>TLS + edge limits
  participant LL as LiteLLM proxy<br/>auth · MCP gateway
  participant PR as Presidio<br/>PII masking
  participant OAI as OpenAI<br/>provider model
  participant XB as Xberg MCP<br/>xberg-sandbox
  participant EG as Egress guard<br/>xberg-dns + Squid
  participant WEB as Allowlisted website<br/>e.g. docs.xberg.io
  participant OBS as Telemetry<br/>spend · metrics · spans

  C->>TR: POST /v1/chat/completions with an mcp tool
  TR->>LL: route by host
  alt key invalid or model not allowed
    LL--xC: 401 / 403 through Traefik
  else authorized
    LL->>PR: pre_call: mask PII in the messages
    PR-->>LL: masked messages
    LL->>XB: MCP tools/list
    XB-->>LL: tool definitions
    Note over LL: keep the servers the key or team may use and the four allowed_tools; in dev, BGE-M3 keeps the top 3 tools
    LL->>OAI: call the model with the tools
    alt model answers without a tool
      OAI-->>LL: completion
    else model calls extract
      OAI-->>LL: tool call: extract(uri)
      LL->>XB: MCP tools/call extract
      XB->>XB: check the URL against the SSRF allowlist
      XB->>EG: resolve the host, HTTPS CONNECT :443
      alt host unlisted, private, or plain HTTP
        EG--xXB: NXDOMAIN or 403 denied
        XB--xLL: tool error, sent to the model as the result
      else host allowlisted
        EG->>WEB: TLS tunnel to the host
        WEB-->>XB: document through the tunnel
        XB-->>LL: extracted text
        LL->>LL: post_mcp_call: mask injection phrases
        Note over LL: dev: a trusted caller's extraction is also indexed in the background (Xberg auto-indexing)
      end
      LL->>OAI: follow-up call with the tool result
      OAI-->>LL: final completion
    end
    LL->>PR: post_call: mask PII in the output
    PR-->>LL: masked output
    LL-)OBS: spend logs, metrics, content-free spans for model and tool calls
    LL-->>TR: response with MCP tool metadata
    TR-->>C: response
  end
